  "body": "### Reproduction steps\n\n**Note**: I'm using podman with a default fedora container provisioned within WSL2, but Zed is running natively on Windows, and so is my shell.\n\nAttempt to open the following Dev Container:\n```\n{\n\t\"name\": \"abcde test\",\n\t\"image\": \"mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/base:debian\",\n\t\"features\": {\n\t\t\"ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/go\": \"1\"\n\t},\n}\n```\n\n### Current vs. Expected behavior\n\nExpected behavior: It should start\nCurrent behavior: The build fails.\n\n### Zed version and system specs\n\nZed: v0.232.3+stable.231.da25b914c25f17ba457abc8cf75b8e42d0b899e2 (Zed) \nOS: Windows 10.0.26200\nMemory: 63.1 GiB\nArchitecture: x86_64\nGPU: AMD Radeon RX 6700 XT || AMD Corporation || 26.3.1 (25.10.43.05-260303a-198974C-AMD-Software-Adrenalin-Edition)\n\n### Attach Zed log file\n\n<details><summary>Zed.log</summary>\n\n```\nERROR [dev_container::devcontainer_manifest] docker buildx build failed: Error: tag abcde_-5780961788c2d36-features: invalid reference format\nERROR [recent_projects::remote_servers] Failed to start dev container: DevContainerUpFailed(\"Failed with nested error: CommandFailed(\\\"podman\\\")\")\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Relevant Zed settings\n\n<details><summary>settings.json</summary>\n\n<!-- Paste your settings inside the code block. -->\n```json\n{\n\t\"use_podman\": true,\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Relevant Keymap\n\n<details><summary>keymap.json</summary>\n\n<!-- Paste your keymap file inside the code block. -->\n```json\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### (for AI issues) Model provider details\n\n_No response_\n\n### If you are using WSL on Windows, what flavor of Linux are you using?\n\nFedora",
